@{5dfdc395425b056c1932da3c|full_name}

Buffer.BlockCopy can only convert a byte array to a float array; 

therefore, converting from a float array to a Vector3 array requires processing within an Udon loop.

```

Vector3 vec3 = new Vector3(floatArray[0], floatArray[1], floatArray[2]);

```

Of course, if Buffer.BlockCopy supported Vector3[] and similar formats, this request would be fulfilled.

@{5f7b354f356ab03255ef6246|full_name}

Small nitpick - `Buffer.BlockCopy` copies bytes to and from arrays of any C# primitive type, not just bytes to floats specifically.  Floats were only used as an example.

Of course, vectors and other Unity structs are not C# primitives, so such methods still don't apply to them.
